      <h2 class="doc-sec__title">Technical FAQ</h2>
      <div class="doc-faq">
        <div class="doc-faq__item">
          <h3 class="doc-faq__q">What are iMosaicArt mosaics made of?</h3>
          <p class="doc-faq__a">Every mosaic is hand-cut from 100% natural marble and stone or from hand-cut vitreous glass, then mounted by hand onto fiber-mesh sheets. Each piece is made to order by a team of 4 to 10 master artisans using traditional Roman hand-cutting techniques — we hold no stock, so your mosaic is created specifically for you.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="doc-faq__item">
          <h3 class="doc-faq__q">Are glass mosaics waterproof?</h3>
          <p class="doc-faq__a">Yes. Our glass tesserae are non-porous and fully waterproof, ideal for swimming pools, fountains, bathrooms, showers, and kitchen backsplashes — they keep their color and integrity even with constant water exposure.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="doc-faq__item">
          <h3 class="doc-faq__q">Can mosaic tiles be installed outdoors?</h3>
          <p class="doc-faq__a">Yes. Made from natural marble, stone, and glass, our mosaics are fully weatherproof and withstand sun, frost, heat, and humidity without fading or cracking — perfect for patios, façades, garden walls, and pool surrounds.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="doc-faq__item">
          <h3 class="doc-faq__q">How thick are the marble and glass tiles?</h3>
          <p class="doc-faq__a">Marble tesserae are typically about 8–10 mm thick and glass about 4 mm, with individual tiles around 15 mm. Because every mosaic is made to order, exact dimensions vary by design — contact us to confirm the specification for a specific piece.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="doc-faq__item">
          <h3 class="doc-faq__q">How are large mosaics delivered and installed?</h3>
          <p class="doc-faq__a">Each mosaic is glued to a fiber-mesh backing that holds the hand-cut tiles together as easy-to-install sheets. Mosaics up to 10 sq. ft. ship in one piece, rolled like a carpet; larger mosaics are split into clearly numbered sections that assemble on site like a puzzle.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="doc-faq__item">
          <h3 class="doc-faq__q">Are the mosaics slip-resistant and safe for floors?</h3>
          <p class="doc-faq__a">Yes. Every mosaic undergoes a slip test before shipping to ensure it is safe for floors, pool surrounds, bathrooms, and other walk-on areas.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="doc-faq__item">
          <h3 class="doc-faq__q">Do iMosaicArt mosaics come with a warranty?</h3>
          <p class="doc-faq__a">Yes — we provide a lifetime warranty on all our mosaics, and every order ships free worldwide.</p>
